  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "You can spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Point\">Force Point</a> to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a>) with the strength of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Force\" title=\"The Force\">The Force</a>, making it resistant to the attacks of other Weapons. Infusing the weapon takes a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Full-Round_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Full-Round Action\">Full-Round Action</a>.<br><br>From that point forward, when you wield the weapon, its <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Damage_Reduction\" title=\"Damage Reduction\">Damage Reduction</a> is doubled, and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsabers\" title=\"Lightsabers\">Lightsabers</a> do not ignore the weapon's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Damage_Reduction\" title=\"Damage Reduction\">Damage Reduction</a>. When you spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Point\">Force Point</a> to modify the attack roll of an <b>Infused Weapon</b>, you also add 2 x the Force Point's result to the damage roll if the attack succeeds.",
